    "model_design": "Remove the auxiliary head (predicting starting-word bigrams) and replace it with a supervised contrastive learning objective on [CLS] embeddings. Specifically, in forward, after obtaining the CLS vector, apply a projection MLP (256-dim hidden, ReLU, output 128-dim embedding). During training, compute contrastive loss (NT-Xent) where positives are same-author samples in the batch. Keep the classification head unchanged. Increase hidden dropout from 0.3 to 0.4 and add stochastic depth with drop rate 0.1 (drop entire layers in DeBERTa encoder probabilistically). This addresses the weak auxiliary signal and overfitting, directly learning author-discriminative embeddings.",
    "training_evaluation": "Switch the optimizer scheduler from cosine warmup to AdamW with OneCycleLR (max_lr=2e-5, pct_start=0.1, final_div_factor=100). Remove the auxiliary loss and set total loss = classification CE + 0.2 * contrastive loss. Keep batch size 16, max length 512, epochs 30, label smoothing 0.1, multi-sample dropout (num_samples=4) during inference. The OneCycleLR stabilizes combined gradient signals and helps convergence."
