{"reason": "The plateau at 0.1886 after 30 epochs suggests we need a systemic change. Success history shows DeBERTa-v3-base with simple scheduler works well, but complexity degrades performance. Tier 3: Integrate pseudo-labeling on test set to leverage unlabeled data, which directly increases effective training size and helps generalization without architectural add-ons. The contrastive loss gave a slight improvement; pseudo-labeling can further reinforce decision boundaries.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Add pseudo-labeling: after training the model on labeled data, use the best model to generate predictions on the test set. Then select high-confidence test samples (max probability > 0.95) and add them to the training set with their predicted labels. Merge train and pseudo-labeled test data, shuffle, and create new dataloaders. This step modifies the dataset used for the second-stage training, keeping the same tokenization and max_length. Ensure the test_df has its text column preserved for inference after pseudo-labeling.", "training_evaluation": "Modify training to run in two stages: first stage: train as before (30 epochs, best model saved). Then load best model, generate test predictions, select confident samples, augment training data. Second stage: continue training on the augmented dataset for another 10 epochs with the same settings (lower initial LR maybe 1e-5) and same early stopping. Save best model. Use that for final validation and test inference. This pseudo-labeling approach uses the test set distribution to improve model robustness, which is likely to break the plateau."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The plateau at 0.1886 after 30 epochs suggests we need a systemic change. Success history shows DeBERTa-v3-base with simple scheduler works well, but complexity degrades performance. Tier 3: Integrate pseudo-labeling on test set to leverage unlabeled data, which directly increases effective training size and helps generalization without architectural add-ons. The contrastive loss gave a slight improvement; pseudo-labeling can further reinforce decision boundaries.",
